# No AGENTS.md rule, deliberately. There was one -- `**/AGENTS.md`, added in
# 3269467 to "hide AGENTS.md" -- and it never hid anything: .gitignore does not
# untrack, so the root file stayed tracked, stayed deployed, and still answers
# 200 at magmacrunch.com/AGENTS.md. This repo is public, so it reads on GitHub
# either way. What the rule did do was make every *new* AGENTS.md invisible to
# git, which is how arcade/SORRY/AGENTS.md went six weeks unnoticed.
# `wiki/` is TRACKED, and was ignored from 2026-07-25 to 2026-10-11 by b165d33a,
# whose message says only "Add wiki/ to .gitignore". Nothing under `wiki/` had
# ever been tracked before that, and `wiki-old-backup/` sits right beside it, so
# the rule was keeping a nested working COPY out of the repo rather than
# deciding this repo should hold no documentation.
#
# It holds it now. The 48 pages under `wiki/` are the source for the published
# wiki, matching `engines/texastoast` and `libs/magmascript`. The clone that
# pushes them is a sibling, `../magmacrunch.com.wiki`, and never a subdirectory
# here -- which is the arrangement the old rule was protecting, and still is.
#
# `dev\wiki-status.py` is what stops the two diverging. This repo is public, so
# its wiki is a real reader surface and the two must agree in BOTH directions;
# CLAUDE.md records 17 pages drifting both ways the last time a loose copy of
# this wiki existed with nothing checking it.
wiki-old-backup/
mcp-server/.venv/
__pycache__/
drafts/

# NOTE: arcade/shared/adenosine-*.js are generated by npm run build:adenosine
# but are deliberately COMMITTED, not ignored.
mcp-server/.env
opencode.json

# Chat/admin shared secret. Lives at ~/arcade-secrets.env on the Pi (outside the
# rsynced tree); never commit a local copy.
*secrets.env

# AI tool artifacts
.aider*
# Claude Code's per-repo state: launch.json, and worktrees/ when a session runs in
# one. .git/info/exclude already covered the worktrees on this machine, but that
# file is local and never leaves it, so a fresh clone had no protection and
# `git add -A` would stage .claude/launch.json.
.claude/

# Historian-tui corrections data (lives in its own repo)
archive/_corrections.*

# Where ci.yml checks the four game repos out for check:gamestamps. Only CI
# makes this, but running those steps by hand should not offer to commit it.
game-repos/
